q q 1 0 0 1 60 706.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 26.5 TD (Every reported field value shall be sanity-checked against the governing boundary conditions of the load case it)Tj -.127706 Tw 0 -12 TD (belongs to before rollup. Reviewers shall confirm this check on the peer-review checklist \(item 9\). A pressure reported)Tj 0 Tw T* (at a scale inconsistent with the case boundary conditions is a defect regardless of unit label.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 628.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 62.5 TD (The check is a scale check, not a unit check. A pressure field whose header reads "Pa" but whose values sit at a)Tj 0 -12 TD (magnitude the boundary conditions cannot produce is defective even if the string "Pa" is technically the intended unit;)Tj T* (the label alone does not vindicate the number. The check is performed at three points in the workflow: \(a\) by the)Tj T* (case-setup engineer immediately after the first converged or first fully-transient output is produced, \(b\) by the rollup)Tj -.109025 Tw T* (engineer at the moment values move from raw fields into summary tables, and \(c\) by the reviewer at peer review. The)Tj 0 Tw T* (reviewer's confirmation is recorded against item 9 of the peer-review checklist for that project.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 598.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 14.5 TD (Sanity checks are performed against the boundary conditions of the )Tj/F4 9.5 Tf (same)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( load case. Cross-case checks are)Tj 0 -12 TD (governed separately by Section 5.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 576.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 11.5 Tf 0 2.5 TD (5. Cross-Case Cross-Checks)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 534.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 14.5 TD (\(5-12 m/s\) are distinct load cases with pressure scales that differ substantially between the two cases. A value)Tj 0 -12 TD (reported from one case shall not be checked against the boundary conditions of the other.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 468.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 50.5 TD (This restriction exists because the two load cases coexist on the same project \(Ocotil